//@version=6
// BTC ATTACK 51 - RSI/PRICE BULLISH DIVERGENCE AT A CONFIRMED SWING LOW.
//
// THE STORED PROMPT says build Attack 37's filter stack, again. THE DOCS OVERRIDE IT, a fifth time:
// Attack 41 closed Attack 37 as a development target, Attack 43 closed the sweep-reversal FAMILY, and
// Attack 47 -- the one filter tried on the current champion, Attack 46 -- died at 24 trades on the same
// ~77% sample wall HARD LESSON 45/49 already named across two labs. The board's own queue (after
// Attacks 47/48/49/50) says stop adding filters on this data and propose a genuinely new mechanism.
// This build also picks up Attack 49's queue item 4: the two mechanisms that cleared 1.0 in this lab
// (the liquidity sweep, the level-target family) both require at least two bars of STRUCTURE, never a
// single-bar trigger. Two single-bar/single-moment ideas (Attack 48 round-number, Attack 49 impulse
// bar) and one two-bar-but-still-price-only idea (Attack 50 session range) have since failed.
//
// ==================== WHAT IS GENUINELY NEW HERE ====================
// Every mechanism on this board so far is built from RAW PRICE: rolling extremes (33), a calendar
// anchor (34/35), a volatility state (36), a failed break of a swing low (37-43), a tap-and-reclaim of
// a swing level (44-47, the champion), a fixed price grid (48), a single bar's own range/volume (49),
// a session's own range (50). NONE of them use a DERIVED OSCILLATOR. This is the first entry in this
// lab conditioned on RSI, not on price structure alone.
//
// CLAIM: when price prints a LOWER swing low but RSI(14) prints a HIGHER low at that same swing
// (classic bullish divergence), the selling pressure driving the new price low is not confirmed by
// momentum -- fewer participants are pushing the move -- and the exhaustion tends to resolve back
// toward the recent trading range rather than extending it further.
//
// ==================== MECHANICS, NO ARRAYS, NO UDFs ====================
// ta.pivotlow(low, leftBars, rightBars) is a built-in (allowlisted) and is NON-REPAINTING: it returns
// a value only on the bar `rightBars` AFTER the actual low, once that low is confirmed by rightBars of
// higher lows on both sides. Two `var float` pairs (not arrays) hold the two most recent confirmed
// pivot lows and the RSI reading at each, shifted by [rightBars] so the RSI value is read from the
// SAME historical bar as the pivot itself, not from the confirmation bar.
//
// AUDIT, one line per leg:
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) - enforced by EXCLUSION via rBig. A divergence whose stop is too close to
//        clear the floor is SKIPPED, never widened.
//   Stop beyond STRUCTURE (LESSON 5) - slPx = lastPivLow, the actual confirmed swing-low PRICE the
//        divergence was measured at. Not an ATR, not a percentage, not the entry price.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6) - LONG ONLY. The mirror (bearish divergence at a swing high) is a
//        DIFFERENT geometry, not built or assumed here; its absence is an outstanding leg, not a
//        design shortcut, per the standing both-directions requirement.
//   BINDING (E17) - divNow requires TWO independently confirmed pivots in a specific relative order;
//        this is expected to bind hard and produce a THIN trade count. Read the count before quoting
//        any ratio (LESSON 12) -- this is flagged as the likely outcome, not discovered after the run.
//   REDUNDANCY (E14) - rBig constrains the STOP distance (an absolute % floor); rrOk only requires the
//        target sit above the entry (a existence check, not a reward-size threshold). They bind on
//        different, non-overlapping quantities.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) - both pivot low and its RSI come from an already-elapsed, confirmed
//        bar ([rightBars] shift); the entry trigger fires on the confirmation bar using only that
//        already-known past data, never a look-ahead.
//   TARGET IS A LEVEL, NOT A MULTIPLE (HARD LESSON 41/47) - tpPx = res, the prior N-bar high, the same
//        validated principle behind the current champion. rr is measured, never set as a parameter.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale.
//
// OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17):
//   * PRE-2024 HALF (H1, never-tuned) BELOW 1.0 -> KILL RULE. Discard, do not run H2, do not filter.
//   * H1 CLEARS 1.0 BUT UNDER ~30 TRADES -> a DIRECTION, not a result (LESSON 12). Report as such,
//        run H2 anyway since credits allow it, but neither half is quotable as a ratio.
//   * BOTH HALVES CLEAR 1.0 WITH A DEFENSIBLE COUNT (>=30 EACH) -> a genuinely new, second family with
//        both halves above 1.0 -- the same bar Attack 37 cleared -- and it queues for the same
//        filter-stack treatment Attack 37 earned, this time on an oscillator-based entry.
//   * A LARGE SHARE OF WINNING HOLDS SIT AT maxBars 192 -> the cap is truncating and the comparison is
//        confounded (HARD LESSON 38); report avgBarsWinning before drawing any conclusion.
//   REPORT avg loser, win rate and max drawdown together on every run (the board's standing
//   instruction after Attack 37 named the three drawdown categories).
strategy("BTC Attack51 RSI divergence swing low", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

leftBars  = input.int(5,   "Pivot left bars")
rightBars = input.int(5,   "Pivot right bars -- confirmation lag")
rsiLen    = input.int(14,  "RSI length")
tgtLook   = input.int(20,  "Target lookback -- prior N-bar high")
minRpct   = input.float(0.80, "Min stop distance as % of price (LESSON 3)")
maxBars   = input.int(192, "Max bars in trade")

rsiVal = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
pl     = ta.pivotlow(low, leftBars, rightBars)

var float lastPivLow = na
var float lastPivRSI = na
var float prevPivLow = na
var float prevPivRSI = na
var bool  divNow      = false

divNow := false
if not na(pl)
    prevPivLow := lastPivLow
    prevPivRSI := lastPivRSI
    lastPivLow := pl
    lastPivRSI := rsiVal[rightBars]
    if not na(prevPivLow) and lastPivLow < prevPivLow and lastPivRSI > prevPivRSI
        divNow := true

res = ta.highest(high, tgtLook)[1]

rLong = close - lastPivLow
minR  = close * minRpct / 100
rBig  = not na(lastPivLow) and rLong >= minR
rrOk  = not na(res) and res > close

goLong = divNow and rBig and rrOk

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := lastPivLow
    tpPx   := res
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(lastPivLow, title="LastPivotLow")
plot(res, title="TargetLevel")
